+# Agent Note: Explorer toggle and file-tree icons/highlighting
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-16-explorer-toggle-and-file-icons.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The file explorer (the details panel's files tab) has no always-available open affordance — a user must first open a tool call's details and switch tabs, so "review the workspace files" is a two-step discovery flow. The file tree also renders bare names with no type icon, and opened text files render as plain text because CodeMirror's `basicSetup` carries no per-language grammar.
+
+## Decision
+
+**Lift the details-tab into the shared chat store, add a session-header explorer toggle, give file rows monochrome extension icons, and detect the editor language from the filename.**
+
+- The details panel's tab choice moves from panel-private `useState` to `detailsTab` on the shared `ChatStoreState` (new `setDetailsTab` action). Every entry point now manages it: the tool-row Details pill sets `tool` before opening, the panel's close button resets to `tool`, and the panel's own tabs write it.
+- A new `ToggleExplorer` entry fills `conversation.session.header.utilities` (registered by ui-conversation, which owns the private store handle). It reads `detailsTab` and either opens the details column on the files tab (`setDetailsTab('files')` + `layout.openDetails()`) or, when already on files, closes it (`setDetailsTab('tool')` + `layout.closeDetails()`). The layout verbs arrive through the entry's inject face.
+- `ui-files` gains a `FileIcon` component: a closed set of monochrome glyphs (`folder`/`code`/`json`/`markdown`/`html`/`css`/`image`/`config`/`text`/`file`) keyed by `fileIconKind(name, type)` over a small extension table. Monochrome `currentColor` strokes keep the token discipline; colored Seti-style icons are deferred.
+- `EditorPane` gains a `filename` prop and resolves a `LanguageSupport` from a small, statically imported set of `@codemirror/lang-*` packages (`javascript`/`json`/`html`/`css`/`markdown`/`python`) keyed by extension, adding it to the view's extensions. `@codemirror/language-data` is rejected because its dynamic `import()` code-splits the single-file client bundle into a chunk the module table cannot resolve.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Panel-private tab state** — smallest change; rejected because an external control (the header toggle) must switch the panel to the files tab, which needs shared state.
+- **A new `detailsOpen` flag in the store** — makes the toggle exactly track open/closed; rejected because it would duplicate the layout store's `details` width, and the tab alone is sufficient for the in-session toggle (the panel X resets it).
+- **Colored Seti-style icons** — the VSCode/PyCharm look; deferred because a colored set needs per-family fill tokens and a larger asset surface, while monochrome glyphs deliver the requested "logo" affordance within the token rules.
+- **`@codemirror/language-data` auto-detection** — one dependency for the full grammar set; rejected because it loads languages through dynamic `import()`, which tsdown code-splits into a relative `require("./dist-*.cjs")` chunk that the single-file client module table cannot resolve. A static `@codemirror/lang-*` map keeps the bundle unsplit at the cost of a smaller grammar set.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- **Bought**: the file explorer is one click away in every session; file rows are visually scannable by type; opened text files get real syntax highlighting without a worker pipeline (still the CodeMirror-over-Monaco stance).
+- **Cost**: `detailsTab` is persisted with the chat store, so a reload that landed on the files tab can make the first toggle click close a not-yet-open panel (the layout width itself is not persisted); the six static `@codemirror/lang-*` grammars grow the client bundle to ~1.6 MB; monochrome icons are a deliberate scope cut from the colored reference look.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `chat-store` spec pins the new `detailsTab` init and `setDetailsTab` action; `selection-survival` updates to the new store shape.
+- `toggle-explorer` spec drives the button on both tabs and asserts the open-files/close layout verbs.
+- `file-icon` spec pins the extension classification (folder collapse, known families, extension-less/trailing-dot fallback) and renders every glyph.
+- `editor-pane` spec mocks the six `@codemirror/lang-*` packages and asserts the matching language is bound, and that unknown and absent filenames bind nothing.
+- Gates: repository typecheck, `test:gui`, `verify-package-invariants`, `verify-cordis-config`, `verify-agent-note-format`, `verify-package-readme-model-experience`.
