+# Agent Note: Split-pane view layout for the conversation center column
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-16-split-pane-view-layout.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The center column renders exactly one conversation view at a time (the `conversation.view` tab ring), so Chat, Trajectory, and Terminal are mutually exclusive and each occupies the full column. There is no way to see two views side by side or stacked, no fullscreen toggle, and no tmux-style split.
+
+## Decision
+
+**Replace the single active-view field with a recursive pane tree in the shared chat store, rendered by a `PaneTree` component with per-pane chrome and draggable dividers.**
+
+- `ChatStoreState.view` (the one active view id) is replaced by three fields: `panes: PaneNode` (a recursive `leaf | split` tree; a split is `row` or `column` with fractional `sizes`), `focusedPaneId`, and `fullscreenPaneId`. New store actions `splitPane`/`closePane`/`setPaneView`/`setPaneSizes`/`setFocusedPane`/`toggleFullscreen`/`switchFocusedTo` wrap pure, immutable tree operations in `pane-tree.ts` (split, close-with-collapse-and-renormalize, leaf view set, split size set, first/focused leaf lookup), so the store stays one write per action.
+- `ConversationSession` renders the tree through `PaneTree` instead of one `renderSlot(..., { only: viewId })`. Each leaf renders its view via the same `conversation.view` slot (`{ only: leaf.viewId }`), and a leaf whose view id is no longer registered falls back to `chat`. The header tab ring now addresses the focused pane (`setPaneView` on its id) and highlights its view, with the same stale-id → `chat` fallback.
+- Each leaf pane has a chrome bar (view label + split right / split down / fullscreen / close). Dividers between split children are pointer-dragged to rebalance the two adjacent fractions (clamped to a 10% minimum, sum preserved).
+- Fullscreen renders only the fullscreen leaf; the same button toggles back to the grid.
+- The chat view's Inspect handoff (`inspectCall`) switches the focused pane to trajectory via `switchFocusedTo` instead of the old `setView`.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **A separate pane store** — keeps the pane layout out of the persisted chat store; rejected because the header, session body, and chat view already share the chat store handle, and persisting the layout per session is a feature (tmux-like) rather than a cost.
+- **CSS grid with fixed cells** — simpler rendering; rejected because recursive arbitrary splitting needs a tree, not a fixed cell count, and per-pane fullscreen/close collapse naturally onto tree operations.
+- **Keep the tab ring and add a fixed two-up mode** — smallest change; rejected because the user asked for full tmux-style recursive splits, which the tree model delivers uniformly.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- **Bought**: Chat/Trajectory/Terminal can be split arbitrarily (right/down), resized by dragging, focused, and taken fullscreen, with the layout persisted per session and the tab ring still driving the focused pane.
+- **Cost**: the store shape change (`view` → `panes`/`focusedPaneId`/`fullscreenPaneId`) ripples into the header, session body, and the `inspectCall` handoff; multiple panes of the same view share that view's store (two Chat panes share selection/draft); fullscreen/focus persist across reloads with the tree.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `pane-tree.spec.ts` pins the pure operations (split, close-with-collapse, size renormalization, view/size set, first/focused leaf).
+- `chat-store.spec.ts` and `selection-survival.spec.ts` pin the new store shape and the pane actions.
+- `pane-tree.client.spec.tsx` drives the renderer: leaf/split/fullscreen rendering, chrome verbs, and divider drag rebalancing.
+- `skeleton.client.spec.tsx` and `ui-trajectory/views.client.spec.tsx` update to the pane actions and the new session locale seat; the stale-view fallback is asserted via `switchFocusedTo('removed-view')`.
+- Gates: repository typecheck, `test:gui`, `verify-package-invariants`, `verify-cordis-config`, `verify-agent-note-format`.
